                <pb facs="0865" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg779"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that he called upon the Turkish minister for foreign
                    affairs on September 9 and made a formal demand that the present governor of
                    Beirut be removed on the ground that it was deemed impossible to secure proper
                    protection for the lives and property of American citizens under his
                    administration. Mr. Leishman is inclined to believe that the demand will receive
                    prompt and favorable consideration.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
